error[ffi_lock_copied]: this copies a `Box`, whose C struct `struct box` holds a `pthread_mutex_t` at `m`, which C forbids to copy
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2136-a-value-only-the-probe-sees-is-told-beside-a-copied-lock.hero:18:14
     |
  18 |     boxes = [Box(n: 1, rest: zero)]  #~ ffi_lock_copied
     |              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: a copy of a lock is a second lock holding the first one's state: the copy of a held mutex reads held, and unlocking one leaves the other locked
  note: an array or a map holds its elements by value, so each element is a copy: keep each record in a cell of its own, `c: T @= T(...)`, and lend it with `@`
  note: lend the place instead: a function taking `c: T lent` reads the caller's own cell and changes nothing, `f(c)`; one taking `@c` may change it, `f(@c)`; a field is read in place, `c.n`

error[ffi_constant_type]: `K_DIV` in `fixedbugs-2128-values.h` cannot be declared `i64`: clang refuses the header's value at line 4: its expression holds an operation C leaves undefined for the operands it is given, and the program's own unit, built with clang's checks for an overflow, a shift, a division by zero and a float out of an integer's range, traps where it reads it
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2136-a-value-only-the-probe-sees-is-told-beside-a-copied-lock.hero:15:5
     |
  15 |     constant K_DIV: i64  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-2128-values.h` line 4 reads `#define K_DIV ((-2147483647 - 1) / -1)`
  note: an operation C leaves undefined gives no value: wherever C computes it, a program reading `K_DIV` reads whatever the machine held. A group's `constant` is the value C computes from the header (§ 13): correct the value there, or bind a constant whose value C defines
